{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer","id":1124364,"title":"Kickstarter Update! Chargen and Revised Netjer!!!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-03T10:28:55-07:00","id":1124364,"title":"Kickstarter Update! Chargen and Revised Netjer!!!","content":"I'm getting ready to go to work right now, but I definitely wanted to get the conversation started on this Update. <br /> <br /> \u200bThe Chargen stuff looks nice and straightforward at first glance. I really like the collaborative nature of Deeds. I just love imagining my group sitting around our table, tossing ideas back and forth about how our respective Deeds and goals can mix together into serving the ST's story more completely.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Netjer? A vast improvement over the first draft! I love just about all the changes. I'm so glad to see Aset is back to being a solo act, because she really deserves it in my book. Het-Heru is very cool too. The Netjer are officially back on &quot;Favorite Pantheon&quot; list. Really great stuff. <br /> <br /> \u200bHere's the Chargen link:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kd2NPYUpYNm52OUU/view\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kd2NPYUpYNm52OUU/view\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kd2NPYUpYNm52OUU/view\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kd2NPYUpYNm52OUU/view </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And the Netjer:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1se3dKukzSy4Bi331sDwYwb2rBdmFuVwPabVFpfb1V8s/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1se3dKukzSy4Bi331sDwYwb2rBdmFuVwPabVFpfb1V8s/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1se3dKukzSy4Bi331sDwYwb2rBdmFuVwPabVFpfb1V8s/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1se3dKukzSy4Bi331sDwYwb2rBdmFuVwPabVFpfb1V8s/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T11:19:35-07:00","id":1124397,"title":"","content":"Salivating over the deeds to distract myself from the fact that the Calling section isn't part of the preview. ;_;<br /> <br /> It's very interesting that Knacks can be purchased for 2XP though. I would have thought they'd be more expensive to get than skills.<br /> <br /> And have Approaches been mentioned before?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T11:32:14-07:00","id":1124407,"title":"","content":"Deeds and Aspirations are the same thing right? Am I the only one who finds that it would be better if they stuck to one consistently for readability's sake? That aside, I find it interesting that Callings are a part of Origins... I always thought they were something that Scions got post Visitation like Purviews and would be a part of Hero... then again, there are apparently Mortal and Immortal Knacks for Callings, so maybe Visitation is only needed for the latter... also since Origins allows non Scion characters, this does seem to imply that mortals have Callings as well... either way it just made Origins level play more interesting for me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T11:32:29-07:00","id":1124408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1124397#post1124397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Salivating over the deeds to distract myself from the fact that the Calling section isn't part of the preview. ;_;<br /> <br /> It's very interesting that Knacks can be purchased for 2XP though. I would have thought they'd be more expensive to get than skills.<br /> <br /> And have Approaches been mentioned before?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, at 2 experience, it's going to take an average of about 1 - 2 sessions per knack you want to buy. So it seems like a steady increase, to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T12:08:08-07:00","id":1124423,"title":"","content":"The deeds are neat... The ability to shuffle your points around between sessions is neat...<br /> <br /> Wait. *Scrolls back up*<br /> <br /> ... <i>SCION DOESN'T HAVE SCALING EXPERIENCE COSTS!</i> Getting your fifth dot of Strength/Might costs the same as getting your second! WOOOOOO!<br /> <br /> Alright, time to sink my teeth into the Netjer. While I'm not a scholar... I have to say I see a LOT of potential in these write-ups.<br /> <br /> Also, one of my friends noted that he likes the image of Set being a sitcom Overprotective Dad of a rebellious daughter, and the image makes me laugh <i>endlessly</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T13:18:01-07:00","id":1124450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1124423#post1124423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, one of my friends noted that he likes the image of Set being a sitcom Overprotective Dad of a rebellious daughter, and the image makes me laugh <i>endlessly</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Looks at my group</i><br /> <br /> This is good and you should all feel good because this is going to cause so much fun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T13:56:32-07:00","id":1124461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1124450#post1124450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is good and you should all feel good because this is going to cause so much fun</div> </div> </div> </div>I have some of the best players a ST could ask for, seriously. Mostly they go for &quot;Character idea --&gt; Figure out how to build this mechanically&quot; rather than &quot;Oh this class/build looks sweet, I'll figure out a personality later&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T18:48:55-07:00","id":1124567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1124407#post1124407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deeds and Aspirations are the same thing right? Am I the only one who finds that it would be better if they stuck to one consistently for readability's sake?</div> </div> </div> </div>As near as I can tell, yes. They probably have to change some terminology because OPP is only licensing <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> while they out-right own the <i>Scion</i> IP. But, than again, they were the ones who did the new editions that use Aspirations so I really don't have an answer....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1124423#post1124423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... <i>SCION DOESN'T HAVE SCALING EXPERIENCE COSTS!</i> Getting your fifth dot of Strength/Might costs the same as getting your second! WOOOOOO!</div> </div> </div> </div>OPP did the same thing to <i>New World of Darkness</i> when they did the <i>God-Machine</i>/<i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> switch. My group was very happy, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1124461#post1124461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some of the best players a ST could ask for, seriously. Mostly they go for &quot;Character idea --&gt; Figure out how to build this mechanically&quot; rather than &quot;Oh this class/build looks sweet, I'll figure out a personality later&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fortunate in this way, too. We tried a game of 5e D&amp;D as a break one time when not everyone was available and it felt so dumbed-down and flat (and I find 5e an excellent edition compared to some earlier ones).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Man and the Beast are having an amiable picnic in that Savage\u2019s head. It\u2019s rather disturbing.&quot; <i>- Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle, pg. 22</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/145-jsm3050","name":"JSM3050","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:20:06-07:00","id":1124579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JSM3050</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1124567#post1124567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fortunate in this way, too. We tried a game of 5e D&amp;D as a break one time when not everyone was available and it felt so dumbed-down and flat (and I find 5e an excellent edition compared to some earlier ones).</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit that I haven't actually PLAYED 5E, but I'd like to, and I can see a lot of concepts I have working without much adjustment.<br /> <br /> Like, Tiefling Paladin with the Acolyte Background to get my idea of a Tiefling raised in a temple who tries to be as righteous and just as possible to make up for the inherit disadvantage of being a freaking tiefling and thus touched by demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:28:58-07:00","id":1124586,"title":"","content":"Very happy Ma'at is a Primordial. She's a principle the Netjer uphold, not a mythically active actor. At my own table the Netjer are lead officially by the triple crowns of Re in the Overworld, Heru in the World, and Wesir in the Underworld. Unofficially though, Aset is the power behind all three thrones since she possesses Re's name, reanimated Wesir, and has Heru's devotion.... much to Sutekh's frustrated rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-03-2017, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:57:39-07:00","id":1124594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1124586#post1124586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's a principle the Netjer uphold, not a mythically active actor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by what I just read, she'd kind of both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T20:16:34-07:00","id":1124597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1124594#post1124594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Going by what I just read, she'd kind of both.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> She's a being and can manifest as a person, but she's far more abstract than gods in general and doesn't take an active role in Egyptian Myth I'm aware of. So Primordial is the right call IMO.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised Isfet is a Titan and not another Primordial, as Ma'at's opposite. Apep is chaos embodied (i.e. a Titan), Isfet is the abstract concept only occasionally personified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T06:24:53-07:00","id":1124728,"title":"","content":"Maybe Titan can encompass god and primordial scale entities within its umbrella term, representing their domination by their purviews even if they're a living landform rather than just a giant that is also on fire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T09:57:35-07:00","id":1124818,"title":"","content":"I like the Netjer, esp the treatment of the Bast, Bastet, Heru, Sekmet connectiont.<br /> <br /> Under Wesir's description about Nut and Geb's children I think it would make things more clear to list them: Wesir, Set, Aset, and Nephthys. Even though Nephthys isn't getting a write up here, putting relations in context helps.<br /> <br /> I am also concerned about Wadjet being listed as a follower. Wadjet and Nekbet are both associated with the Eye of Re as protectors but also goddesses in thier own right. What kind of being is Wadjet in Scion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3495,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3495-elroar","user":"Elroar","date":". 08-04-2017, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3495-elroar","name":"Elroar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3495_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T10:35:25-07:00","id":1124828,"title":"","content":"Okay Duat sounds horrible, given other Pantheons have better afterlives, less judgemental after lives, why would anyone choose to worship the Netjer over say the Irish Pantheon, especially if they haven't lived the life of a saint?<br /> <br /> Given they are competing for worshippers, you'd think they'd make it easier to get into paradise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T11:08:27-07:00","id":1124840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1124828#post1124828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay Duat sounds horrible, given other Pantheons have better afterlives, less judgemental after lives, why would anyone choose to worship the Netjer over say the Irish Pantheon, especially if they haven't lived the life of a saint?<br /> <br /> Given they are competing for worshippers, you'd think they'd make it easier to get into paradise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not everyone worships the gods for the sake of their afterlife. Sometimes - quite a lot of times, in fact - it's about what the gods can do for them in their mortal life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T11:22:20-07:00","id":1124845,"title":"","content":"Don't see what's so bad about Duat? A'aru sounds like your typical idyllic paradise for the worthy. Not everyone proves worthy, of course, but that's true of all the ancient religions. It certainly doesn't sound any worse than &quot;Be superhuman or languish for eternity as a nameless zombie&quot; (Greek,) or &quot;Die in glorious combat or be condemned to the cruelties of Hel's hall&quot; (Norse,) or &quot;Sacrifice yourself or be condemned to another meaningless eternity&quot; (Aztec.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T11:34:46-07:00","id":1124850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1124828#post1124828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay Duat sounds horrible, given other Pantheons have better afterlives, less judgemental after lives, why would anyone choose to worship the Netjer over say the Irish Pantheon, especially if they haven't lived the life of a saint?<br /> <br /> Given they are competing for worshippers, you'd think they'd make it easier to get into paradise.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how most ancient worship works. Winning worship by promising better afterlives was a small mystery cult thing until Christianity took it mainstream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T12:27:42-07:00","id":1124878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1124845#post1124845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't see what's so bad about Duat? A'aru sounds like your typical idyllic paradise for the worthy. Not everyone proves worthy, of course, but that's true of all the ancient religions. It certainly doesn't sound any worse than &quot;Be superhuman or languish for eternity as a nameless zombie&quot; (Greek,) or &quot;Die in glorious combat or be condemned to the cruelties of Hel's hall&quot; (Norse,) or &quot;Sacrifice yourself or be condemned to another meaningless eternity&quot; (Aztec.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In regards to the Norse, I've actually read from some sources that while Hel primarily punished the unworthy dead there was another aspect of her duties that including &quot;Supplying the dead with lodgings and belongings&quot;. It seems that, while Nefilhem was not a fun place and Hel was not a particularly nice lady, most people that didn't die a glorious death fell into more, servant roles with the torment being reserved for things like kinslayers.<br /> <br /> Granted I am not sure of how accurate that source is and it's been awhile since I've read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T12:50:58-07:00","id":1124898,"title":"","content":"I will admit that Bast/Bastet being divided into seperate gods rather than a mantle is off putting to me, mostly because bastet was made into a seperate unlisted god and one of my players was thinking of a bastet scion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T13:07:40-07:00","id":1124908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1124828#post1124828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay Duat sounds horrible, given other Pantheons have better afterlives, less judgemental after lives, why would anyone choose to worship the Netjer over say the Irish Pantheon, especially if they haven't lived the life of a saint?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, at least with the Nejter, Anpu/Anubis will escort you to the scales. Like, yeah, Duat's dangerous, but the Nejter give enough of a fuck to tell a major god &quot;Keep the souls safe until they're judged&quot;.<br /> <br /> Like, don't the Theoi basically just say &quot;YOU get there. Have some money for the ferryman&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T13:18:48-07:00","id":1124914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1124828#post1124828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay Duat sounds horrible, given other Pantheons have better afterlives, less judgemental after lives, why would anyone choose to worship the Netjer over say the Irish Pantheon, especially if they haven't lived the life of a saint?<br /> <br /> Given they are competing for worshippers, you'd think they'd make it easier to get into paradise.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not like you get a brochure telling you about the afterlife benefits of each religion. You get stories, stories that joe schmoe the kemeticist isn't necessarily able to prove or disprove. He might have been born into it or converted for other reasons anyway.<br /> <br /> Most people haven't lived the lives of saints, but that doesn't mean that they opportunistically seek out another faith to escape some kind of perdition or unpleasantness. One might even hazard a guess that sort of thing probably doesn't work. :P It's not really how faith works in real life anyway, and despite the weirdness of the World, it doesn't sound like people vacation in Duat to tell one another that there's better real estate in other afterlives. Maybe <i>your </i>character does that, to be clear, but <i>people </i>don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 08-04-2017, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T13:35:18-07:00","id":1124919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1124898#post1124898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will admit that Bast/Bastet being divided into seperate gods rather than a mantle is off putting to me, mostly because bastet was made into a seperate unlisted god and one of my players was thinking of a bastet scion</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on the write up I think that you could mechanically represent Bastet with Bast's callings and purviews. They are different godesses, but close enough for confusion to happen. From what we've been told you inherit one calling and one purview from your parent so in most cases it would work, I think, kinda, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T13:49:16-07:00","id":1124927,"title":"","content":"Could someone please explain to me what the distinction between Bast and Bastet is in the original myth? I was almost certain that they were completely interchangeable names for exactly the same goddess, and I'm admittedly a splitter rather than a lumper when it comes to mythological beings. Sekhmet I totally understand the distinction for, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T14:44:01-07:00","id":1124955,"title":"","content":"What's a &quot;Favored Approach&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T17:21:14-07:00","id":1125011,"title":"","content":"The writeup says that The Netjer and the Teotl get along well enough.<br /> <br /> \u200bHowever? There is one.......possible......major conflict between them. Tlaloc and Sobek. Two crocodilian river gods from pyramid-building cultures. One likes to protect children. The other likes to have children beaten until they cry and then fed to him.<br /> <br /> \u200bDoes anyone else foresee a kaiju battle when these two meet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T17:35:46-07:00","id":1125014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1124927#post1124927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could someone please explain to me what the distinction between Bast and Bastet is in the original myth? I was almost certain that they were completely interchangeable names for exactly the same goddess, and I'm admittedly a splitter rather than a lumper when it comes to mythological beings. Sekhmet I totally understand the distinction for, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bast and Sekhmet are pretty much indistinguishable. <br /> <br /> Bastet is a nicer kitty goddess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T18:10:41-07:00","id":1125028,"title":"","content":"I always liked Gaiman's take on the whole heart weighed against feather bit, although I have no idea how mythologically accurate it was.<br /> &quot;More [people got into heaven] than you'd think; it was a very heavy feather. We had it specially made.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13075-malicwanderer","name":"MalicWanderer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T19:28:21-07:00","id":1125051,"title":"","content":"Im still not a fan of not using the common names for the Netjer aka Anpu instead of Anubis. It just seems like a poor decision in terms of clarity when the majority of people aren't familiar with these obscure monikers. It feels kinda condescending to me like someone is saying &quot;oh you would understand it if you had minored in north african comparative literature like I did&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T20:06:03-07:00","id":1125064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1125051#post1125051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im still not a fan of not using the common names for the Netjer aka Anpu instead of Anubis. It just seems like a poor decision in terms of clarity when the majority of people aren't familiar with these obscure monikers. It feels kinda condescending to me like someone is saying &quot;oh you would understand it if you had minored in north african comparative literature like I did&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a good thing to spread around their real names, and get more people familiar with them. It's also probably respectful to the culture and the active members of the religion to use the real names. Or at least, as close to the real names as we can get without knowing the exact pronunciation. It's fun, and educational!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T20:06:14-07:00","id":1125065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1125051#post1125051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im still not a fan of not using the common names for the Netjer aka Anpu instead of Anubis. It just seems like a poor decision in terms of clarity when the majority of people aren't familiar with these obscure monikers. It feels kinda condescending to me like someone is saying &quot;oh you would understand it if you had minored in north african comparative literature like I did&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>See, &quot;people need you to use these more pop-culture friendly names or they won't understand&quot; is the position that comes off as condescending to me.<br /> <br /> The Greek names are listed below their Egyptian names, I don't think anyone is going to be confused (though, in the interest of consistency, I'm pretty sure Thoth is Greek - Djehuty should be the primary listed name if they're going with native Egyptian names).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T20:44:50-07:00","id":1125075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1125065#post1125065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Greek names are listed below their Egyptian names, I don't think anyone is going to be confused (though, in the interest of consistency, I'm pretty sure Thoth is Greek - Djehuty should be the primary listed name if they're going with native Egyptian names).</div> </div> </div> </div>On the KS page, Lex did mention this was one of her bigger questions about the update.<br /> <br /> GRANTED, considering how the first draft went down I think it's a sign of improvement where one of the bigger questions/concerns is &quot;Um, why'd you use the Greek name here and nowhere else?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T20:47:21-07:00","id":1125076,"title":"","content":"So, Shu, Tefnut, Geb, and Nut... Primordials? Titans? Gods too distant to make the big 12 list, but who might show up as viable parent/patrons later?<br /> <br /> They could be any if their progenitor was the Primordial Atum, which was presumably (based on Re's write-up) one of the many names of the Primordial creator who Aset reduced to the god Re by stealing his True Name from him. Though I do like my idea of Re fighting Primordials and Titans and seizing their Names as his own in victory, thus making himself retroactively the first being by donning the Name of Atum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-04-2017, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T20:48:03-07:00","id":1125077,"title":"","content":"It sounds like the Bast in the write-up is essentially the deity I usually think of as Sekhmet, while Bastet is the one I think of as Bast/Bastet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T21:04:54-07:00","id":1125080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1125064#post1125064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a good thing to spread around their real names, and get more people familiar with them. It's also probably respectful to the culture and the active members of the religion to use the real names. Or at least, as close to the real names as we can get without knowing the exact pronunciation. It's fun, and educational!</div> </div> </div> </div>But are the Kemetic names the &quot;real&quot; ones? Certainly there are Kemetic followers today in the same vein as Neo Paganism, but these are modern movements picking up the faith from a clean slate without the burden of a continuous evolution from the historical practice of the faith. I'm not trying to begrudge them for choosing to use the names they do, but the last significant historical worship of the Netjer was during the Ptolemic dynasty and they used the greek names, so in my mind in the World of Scion where these ancient faiths were never stomped out by Christianity there was no need for a neo anything movement, and you would think the Greek names would have continued on as the current ones.<br /> <br /> If they use the Kemetic names it should at least be explained IMO, why did they stop using the Ptolemic names? Was there a scism? When and why would a Kemetic movement form in the World? Are there still Ptolemics in Egypt grumbling that their Book of the Dead is the real Book of the Dead and this new age edition is a bunch of hogwash?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T21:32:16-07:00","id":1125091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1125080#post1125080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But are the Kemetic names the &quot;real&quot; ones? Certainly there are Kemetic followers today in the same vein as Neo Paganism, but these are modern movements picking up the faith from a clean slate without the burden of a continuous evolution from the historical practice of the faith. I'm not trying to begrudge them for choosing to use the names they do, but the last significant historical worship of the Netjer was during the Ptolemic dynasty and they used the greek names, so in my mind in the World of Scion where these ancient faiths were never stomped out by Christianity there was no need for a neo anything movement, and you would think the Greek names would have continued on as the current ones.<br /> <br /> If they use the Kemetic names it should at least be explained IMO, why did they stop using the Ptolemic names? Was there a scism? When and why would a Kemetic movement form in the World? Are there still Ptolemics in Egypt grumbling that their Book of the Dead is the real Book of the Dead and this new age edition is a bunch of hogwash?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think Kemeticism ever stopped in the World. The Ptolemaic cultural lens was always distinct to the Greek speaking ruling class who didn't even know the language of their subjects for the most part (Cleopatra was remarkable out of her family in that regard - actively speaking the language, garbing herself in the clothes of, and visibly practicing the religion of her people too gain their loyalty).<br /> <br /> Now, I do think it's possible that a hybrid religion like the Cult of Isis (basically reskinned Eleucinian Mysteries around Isis's resurrection of Osiris rather than Persephone returning from the Underworld) may exist and use the Greek names, sure! But the deeply culturally Kemetic believers who care about concepts like Ma'at and Isfet, they're going to use Kemetic names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-05-2017, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T22:01:37-07:00","id":1125097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1125091#post1125091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't think Kemeticism ever stopped in the World. The Ptolemaic cultural lens was always distinct to the Greek speaking ruling class who didn't even know the language of their subjects for the most part (Cleopatra was remarkable out of her family in that regard - actively speaking the language, garbing herself in the clothes of, and visibly practicing the religion of her people too gain their loyalty).<br /> <br /> Now, I do think it's possible that a hybrid religion like the Cult of Isis (basically reskinned Eleucinian Mysteries around Isis's resurrection of Osiris rather than Persephone returning from the Underworld) may exist and use the Greek names, sure! But the deeply culturally Kemetic believers who care about concepts like Ma'at and Isfet, they're going to use Kemetic names.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also just think it is going to be annoying for what is likely the vast majority of people who are only familiar with the Greek names to have to try and cross reference every time a Egyptian god gets mentioned going forward in the Scion gameline. Using the Greek names as the in text standard would be clearer for likely 90% of the people playing if I was making a educated guess. This forum is not very representative of the adverage players knowledge, its a bunch of mythology super nerds which is great, but when I asked the half dozen people I actually play Scion with if they know who these Kemetic gods are by name they just stare at me blankly. If I ask them who Anubis or Osiris are they immediately know who they are and what they are about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T22:06:28-07:00","id":1125099,"title":"","content":"I really think you're overestimating how hard these names are to learn and recognize. They're all pretty similar (Djehuty being an outlier).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T22:29:51-07:00","id":1125104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1125011#post1125011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The writeup says that The Netjer and the Teotl get along well enough.<br /> <br /> \u200bHowever? There is one.......possible......major conflict between them. Tlaloc and Sobek. Two crocodilian river gods from pyramid-building cultures. One likes to protect children. The other likes to have children beaten until they cry and then fed to him.<br /> <br /> \u200bDoes anyone else foresee a kaiju battle when these two meet?</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, Sebek is also extremely ruthless and brutal by his admission. They may not agree on the whole children thing, but they're more similar than different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T23:15:21-07:00","id":1125115,"title":"","content":"I see no issue with using the correct names for the Netjer. I would presume that the same will be done for other Pantheon as well (especially the many First Nations ones). The familiar western name is given for each, so it's not hard to connect them. Use whatever you like in your own game, certainly, but I'm a fan of the correct names being used.<br /> <br /> Bast is the early lioness Goddess of Protection: Bastet would be the &quot;Perfumed One&quot; who was associated with festivals and beauty.<br /> <br /> And I'm happy with the new version of the Netjer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T23:19:42-07:00","id":1125117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1125104#post1125104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, Sebek is also extremely ruthless and brutal by his admission. They may not agree on the whole children thing, but they're more similar than different.</div> </div> </div> </div>How similar they are just makes them more disposed to be rivals, with that major difference being the sparking issue for conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T23:52:06-07:00","id":1125121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1125104#post1125104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, Sebek is also extremely ruthless and brutal by his admission. They may not agree on the whole children thing, but they're more similar than different.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bTrue, but if Sobek has a preferred protectorate and Tlaloc likes to prey upon that protectorate, that's a pretty solid environment in which to grow a rivalry. Sobek may not spend a lot of time hunting Tlaloc down, but if they cross paths, Sobek would at the very least have some choice words for him. And Heaven help Tlaloc if Sobek comes across him when he's actually presiding over one of his sacrifices. <br /> <br /> \u200bSeems like a likely scenario anyway.<br /> <br /> \u200bWith regard to the name issue? I do like the idea of giving the Greek and Egyptian names for the gods. I personally don't think that the gods mind their Greek names at all. They're just another name by which they were invoked. I don't think the Netjer had a very big problem with the Greek conquest at all. Alexander the Great went through the process of being crowned as a proper Egyptian Pharaoh and showed a lot of respect to the Egyptians and their ways. He didn't suppress or try to subvert their religion. Heck, he actually helped to SPREAD the religion of the Netjer. <br /> <br /> \u200bThe Greek names were just the names by which the Greeks came to know the Netjer. I doubt they forced the Egyptians to only use the Greek names in their daily lives. So, for the most part, I imagine the Netjer are okay with being addressed by either name. They may be impressed with you if you use their Egyptian names since that implies that you've actually done some research on them and are making an effort to impress or flatter them, but that's about the main difference. <br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough? I do imagine that in current events, Aset very much does NOT like her Greek name right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":679,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","user":"unnatural1","date":". 08-05-2017, 03:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T03:11:25-07:00","id":1125154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1125121#post1125121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAlthough? I do imagine that in current events, Aset very much does NOT like her Greek name right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>That alone might actually be reason enough to prefer the Kemetic names in the text, just for sake of dodging bullets.<br /> <br /> Personally, while I had no familiarity at all with the Kemetic names before reading this update I didn't find it too hard to follow along. Usually they were similar enough I could more or less tell who they were talking about by context. I imagine it would be similar for others with a passing familiarity with the myths using only the Greek names. And of course there's always the listed aliases to fall back on. Perhaps the index should include listings for the Greek names, just to assist finding the right write up if you've forgotten the Kemetic name to look for? Actually I'd support that for most common aliases, regardless of pantheon, if there's room.<br /> <br /> I agree with the idea that it should probably list Nut and Geb's children at some point, especially since Nephthys (which I'm guessing is her Greek name?) isn't mentioned anywhere else I think. Tho I feel like that's probably the thing I'd personally want to see changed. If nothing else maybe a mention of her part in helping Aset with the whole Wesir/Set/Heru debacle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13075-malicwanderer","name":"MalicWanderer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T03:32:23-07:00","id":1125160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalicWanderer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1125154#post1125154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nephthys (which I'm guessing is her Greek name?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Nebthet or Neber-Het would be the Kemetic (or as close as we can manage).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T06:50:28-07:00","id":1125197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1125160#post1125160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nebthet or Neber-Het would be the Kemetic (or as close as we can manage).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I didn't know Nephthys' kemetic name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3495-elroar","name":"Elroar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3495_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T17:19:57-07:00","id":1125421,"title":"","content":"While I will fully admit that I personally will continue to use the Greek and/or Latin names for the Egyptian gods (mostly because they are ingrained into my mind at this point), I still appreciate the attempt to use the closest thing we can get to their original names. Overall, I love the changes, and while there are some things I personally would change, I think its a massive improvement and I appreciate them listening to everyone's concerns and making some alterations. Still though, come on now! Nephthys needs some love!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13472-~nkf~","name":"~NKF~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T05:22:49-07:00","id":1125549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1124878#post1124878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In regards to the Norse, I've actually read from some sources that while Hel primarily punished the unworthy dead there was another aspect of her duties that including &amp;quot;Supplying the dead with lodgings and belongings&amp;quot;. It seems that, while Nefilhem was not a fun place and Hel was not a particularly nice lady, most people that didn't die a glorious death fell into more, servant roles with the torment being reserved for things like kinslayers.<br /> <br /> Granted I am not sure of how accurate that source is and it's been awhile since I've read it.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'll also point out that women who died in child birth also went to the Norse Paradise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T05:31:45-07:00","id":1125553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1124850#post1124850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not how most ancient worship works. Winning worship by promising better afterlives was a small mystery cult thing until Christianity took it mainstream.</div> </div> </div> </div> That explains, ancient Times but now it competes directly with Christianity, were all you need to do is ask for forgiveness and your good to avoid the bad place. <br /> <br /> And yes some of the other religions have dark sides in the afterlife, but many don't like the Yoruba or the Danaan.<br /> <br /> Most religions modernize and I just don't see the Netjer not updating its afterlife to be more competive.<br /> <br /> And the whole Bast/Bastet/Sekmet thing is confusing, I'll have to reread it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T08:27:13-07:00","id":1125605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1125553#post1125553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That explains, ancient Times but now it competes directly with Christianity, were all you need to do is ask for forgiveness and your good to avoid the bad place.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Psh, how great can the Christian Heaven be if they let in any jackass that says 'I killed a person, my bad!'?&quot;<br /> <br /> (To be clear, that snarky quip does not reflect my personal beliefs, I was being snarky for demonstration's sake)<br /> <br /> To be a bit more serious... The Nejter afterlife doesn't sound too much worse than the Christian afterlife. You die and then wait in line to be judged based on your sins and virtues in life. One has someone look up a big record of your life, the other weighs your heart against a magic feather.<br /> <br /> Then depending, either you're in and you go to the nice afterlife, or you're not and you're SOL. And honestly, are the wastes of Duat that much worse than the Christian fire and brimstone Hell?<br /> <br /> Besides, I don't know if many religious people shop around for religions based solely on perks. There could be any number of reasons in The World for following one religion besides &quot;Well I can sin my ass off and if I confess I'm gold&quot;<br /> <br /> For Example: The worshipper grew up hearing the stories of the Nejter and felt a kinship to them; they could just have learned about them in a religion class in high school and thought that Sehkmet is pretty boss, so they'll see if there's a temple to her in town; Perhaps a Scion of Anubis personally made sure that their grandfather's soul made it through Dust safely, and now this person honors the Nejter out of gratitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 08-06-2017, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T16:21:59-07:00","id":1126096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1125605#post1125605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Psh, how great can the Christian Heaven be if they let in any jackass that says 'I killed a person, my bad!'?&quot;<br /> <br /> (To be clear, that snarky quip does not reflect my personal beliefs, I was being snarky for demonstration's sake)<br /> <br /> To be a bit more serious... The Nejter afterlife doesn't sound too much worse than the Christian afterlife. You die and then wait in line to be judged based on your sins and virtues in life. One has someone look up a big record of your life, the other weighs your heart against a magic feather.<br /> <br /> Then depending, either you're in and you go to the nice afterlife, or you're not and you're SOL. And honestly, are the wastes of Duat that much worse than the Christian fire and brimstone Hell?<br /> <br /> Besides, I don't know if many religious people shop around for religions based solely on perks. There could be any number of reasons in The World for following one religion besides &quot;Well I can sin my ass off and if I confess I'm gold&quot;<br /> <br /> For Example: The worshipper grew up hearing the stories of the Nejter and felt a kinship to them; they could just have learned about them in a religion class in high school and thought that Sehkmet is pretty boss, so they'll see if there's a temple to her in town; Perhaps a Scion of Anubis personally made sure that their grandfather's soul made it through Dust safely, and now this person honors the Nejter out of gratitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I remember, the Duat can be pretty trippy as you're heading in, but once you're judged worthy, it's a pretty decent place, resembling a ghostly version of the real world without the downsides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T20:24:06-07:00","id":1126151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1125553#post1125553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That explains, ancient Times but now it competes directly with Christianity, were all you need to do is ask for forgiveness and your good to avoid the bad place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure if you're willing to assume the promise Christianity is offering exists. But that's putting the cart before the horse. If you have other beliefs instead you're going to focus on the hard work to get into A'aru, rather than assume this easier path to salvation is real.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, Christianity being largely unique at the time with its open promise of paradise contributed massively to its spread, and that can still have happened in the World. Christianity is still the majority faith in the western World. But I don't find it harder to fathom some Kemetics not converting based on its promises than Jews who refused to convert for Christianity's promises, instead upholding the heavier legal traditions of their ancestor with hope for a beneficial eventual resurrection, but with a pretty bleak afterlife in the meantime (Sheol).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-08-2017, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T00:39:14-07:00","id":1126212,"title":"","content":"If you become a christian just so you can sin as much as you want and plan to &quot;repent&quot; on your deathbed its not going to work. Repentance has to be legitimate not gaming the system. If you want to game the system its the Celestial Bureaucracy all the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T01:40:19-07:00","id":1126221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1125553#post1125553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That explains, ancient Times but now it competes directly with Christianity, were all you need to do is ask for forgiveness and your good to avoid the bad place. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of non Christians in the real world who follow other religions for one reason or the other... There's no reason the World is any different in that regard. Not everybody in the world automatically jumps to the easiest path... Speaking of, I'm no Christian theologian, and please correct me if I'm wrong, but doesn't the repentance have to be genuine? Feeling actual repentance for sin is hardly the easy way out.<br /> <br /> Also, seriously... The afterlife where a bunch of fairly nice gods judge your deeds and reward or punish you accordingly with paradise or simple oblivion is not remotely the worst afterlife out there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T02:00:09-07:00","id":1126222,"title":"","content":"Honestly, if paradise or non-existence are the options rather than paradise or eternal suffering, the Egyptian afterlife is the one I'd prefer greatly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T02:14:01-07:00","id":1126625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1125553#post1125553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the whole Bast/Bastet/Sekmet thing is confusing, I'll have to reread it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ancient Egyptian gods are confusing. Neall's trying to account for how Bast was a lion headed goddess indistinguishable from Sekhmet except in name (Bast was in lower egypt, Sekhmet was in upper egypt), until later there was a kitty guardian goddess associated with perfume, around the same time the additional feminine suffex was added, so that's Bastet.<br /> <br /> My own inclination would be to have Bast/et be primarily the guardian cat goddess, and then the Sekhmet mantle she shares with Het-Heru is the war goddess with all those traits that were identical between Bast and Sekhmet. But that's just my table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T02:22:11-07:00","id":1126628,"title":"","content":"Also, the writeup of Set made me imagine a Scion of Set talking about how Set is the most effective guardian of Re's barge, how Set has chased off and driven back Apep more than any other Netjer, and how he once cut the World from Apep's belly. And then...<br /> <br /> Tuatha Scion: ... Um, didn't Set kill Osiris, cut him to pieces, and put out one of Horus's eyes?<br /> <br /> Set Scion: Okay first of all, they prefer the names Wesir and Heru, respectively. Secondly, well, my roommate never does the dishes. Nobody's <i>perfect</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T03:11:29-07:00","id":1126640,"title":"","content":"The view of Set is one of the big divides between the two largest Kemetic religions I'm imagining using at my own table. The Cult of Isis is the most widespread Kemetic faith, focuses of the resurrection of Osiris (uses the Ptolemaic names obviously), the promise of a more benevolent afterlife, and presents Set as pretty much the devil. The Cult of Re is the largest Kemetic faith and unlike the Cult of Isis it is concentrated in Egypt (tying roughly in numbers with Christianity for second largest religion in the country after Islam), and focuses faith on Re's nightly struggle against Apep and the balance of Ma'at and Ifset. To the Cult of Re, Sutekh is a champion over Ifset and protector of Re.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T20:09:31-07:00","id":1126941,"title":"","content":"Just thinking, Khonsu is another good candidate for a Titan. He's the direct offspring of Amun (a Primordial) who is directly evoked in the Cannibal Hymn to hunt and consume other gods. Assuming he's the &quot;Moon&quot; Djehuty gambles with to win days, that also places him as someone the Netjer had to best to control.<br /> <br /> So with Khonsu, you have a Moon Titan, a Sun Titan (Aten), and a primordial chaos Titan (Apep)<br /> <br /> [still inclined to count Ifset herself as a Primordial opposite number to Ma'at rather than a Titan]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T21:39:37-07:00","id":1126956,"title":"","content":"I'm back! In brief: the Netjer rewrite is vastly improved, with special mention going out to how perfectly whoever wrote this got my beloved Het-Heru! My gripes are incredibly minor; Uesir letting the dead out of Duat feels a little odd to me, Wepawet is a wolf hunting deity who is Anpu's son rather than another name for him, and I'm not sure why Djehuti got saddled with his Greek name. Super excited happy to see how well this was done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T06:09:52-07:00","id":1127078,"title":"","content":"I agree that Wepawet should be separated from Anpu so that he could possibly be included later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T06:18:11-07:00","id":1127083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1126956#post1126956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm back! In brief: the Netjer rewrite is vastly improved, with special mention going out to how perfectly whoever wrote this got my beloved Het-Heru! My gripes are incredibly minor; Uesir letting the dead out of Duat feels a little odd to me, Wepawet is a wolf hunting deity who is Anpu's son rather than another name for him, and I'm not sure why Djehuti got saddled with his Greek name. Super excited happy to see how well this was done.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWelcome back, Lex! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bAnd yeah, I agree about Wepawet. The good news is that it would be easy enough to include Wepawet in a later book and just explain that people mistake Wepawet and Anpu as being one and the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T06:24:38-07:00","id":1127087,"title":"","content":"All in all, I love this write-up, it even taught me a few things I didn't know about Egyptian mythology, but I still have a list a mile long of Egyptian gods I'd like to see added in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T10:27:53-07:00","id":1127190,"title":"","content":"The big 5 to still address (though some might be Primordials or Titans, but they'd still demand coverage) would be Shu, Tefnut, Keb, Nut, and Neber-Het<br /> <br /> Which is not to say i don't want to see Bes, Renenutet, Nekhbet &amp; Wadjet, the 4 sons of Heru, etc etc - just that those first five are the current biggest holes in the major mythos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T11:58:18-07:00","id":1127230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1126956#post1126956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm back! In brief: the Netjer rewrite is vastly improved, with special mention going out to how perfectly whoever wrote this got my beloved Het-Heru!</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I snickered at the note saying that the biggest romantic difficulty that Scions of Het-Heru have comes from having too many loves at once, mostly since in the Exalted game I'm in that could apply to both my character and another PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T13:10:19-07:00","id":1127266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1127230#post1127230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit I snickered at the note saying that the biggest romantic difficulty that Scions of Het-Heru have comes from having too many loves at once, mostly since in the Exalted game I'm in that could apply to both my character and another PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you think I felt? My fursona started off as a brainstorm of a Scion of Het-Heru and is now canonically dating like five other characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T13:13:09-07:00","id":1127269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1127266#post1127266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you think I felt? My fursona started off as a brainstorm of a Scion of Het-Heru and is now canonically dating like five other characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess: A deep-set sense of <i>utter vindication</i>. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T13:32:37-07:00","id":1127286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1127269#post1127269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My guess: A deep-set sense of <i>utter vindication</i>. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>In all seriousness: she's one of my favorite mythological figures and the only one who's ever answered a prayer of mine, and I'm overjoyed to not only see her in the book, but done well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T19:00:22-07:00","id":1127437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1126941#post1126941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just thinking, Khonsu is another good candidate for a Titan. He's the direct offspring of Amun (a Primordial) who is directly evoked in the Cannibal Hymn to hunt and consume other gods. Assuming he's the &amp;quot;Moon&amp;quot; Djehuty gambles with to win days, that also places him as someone the Netjer had to best to control.<br /> <br /> So with Khonsu, you have a Moon Titan, a Sun Titan (Aten), and a primordial chaos Titan (Apep)<br /> <br /> [still inclined to count Ifset herself as a Primordial opposite number to Ma'at rather than a Titan]</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct me if I am wrong but Djehuty's write up sounds like they have incorporated Khonsu into his mantle. And that Het Heru gambled with Djehuty directly for more days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3495-elroar","name":"Elroar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3495_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T20:28:42-07:00","id":1127461,"title":"","content":"Let me go reread!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T20:39:36-07:00","id":1127467,"title":"","content":"&quot;Some scraps with the gods of Canaan&quot;<br /> <br /> That's a casual way to refer to waters turning to blood, boils, lice, locusts, fiery hail, pestilence, rampaging wild beasts, 3 days darkness, and the death of all the firstborn sons in Egypt...<br /> <br /> (There were also frogs, but I'm not sure those actually bothered the Egyptians to whom the frog was a fertility symbol of the Nile's annual flooding)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T20:48:41-07:00","id":1127470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elroar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1127437#post1127437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct me if I am wrong but Djehuty's write up sounds like they have incorporated Khonsu into his mantle. And that Het Heru gambled with Djehuty directly for more days.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just went back to check - it's ambiguous. It says that Djehuty brokered enough extra moonlight for the extra days. It does make it sound on brief glance like he was being brokered with for the time, but actually then it would say &quot;the Goddess (Nut) brokered enough extra moonlight&quot; but it says &quot;the God&quot; (Djehuty). So he was brokering with someone on her behalf - which would presumably be Khonsu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T23:20:56-07:00","id":1127503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1127467#post1127467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Some scraps with the gods of Canaan&quot;<br /> <br /> That's a casual way to refer to waters turning to blood, boils, lice, locusts, fiery hail, pestilence, rampaging wild beasts, 3 days darkness, and the death of all the firstborn sons in Egypt...<br /> <br /> (There were also frogs, but I'm not sure those actually bothered the Egyptians to whom the frog was a fertility symbol of the Nile's annual flooding)</div> </div> </div> </div>Could also mean that the Egyptian conquered and lost Canaan several times, incorporated many of the Canaanite gods into their pantheon and even their myths (like Set being offered Anat and Astarte as concubines in the <i>Contendings</i>), and made that famous peace treaty with the Hittites over quarrels over Canaan. Not saying you're wrong, just Egypt had a lot of &quot;scraps&quot; with the Levant, more of a deep, centuries-long relationship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T12:58:21-07:00","id":1127747,"title":"","content":"Ok, on closer review - Shu, Tefnut, Nut, and Geb are mentioned in passing as Primordials.<br /> <br /> They originate from Atum, who was later pulled down to God status in incorporation with Re as Aset stole Re's Name. So that fits Re being a historically late god of to rise in real history, but mythicaly being the first.<br /> <br /> I assume Khepri and Atum-Re are Mantles of Re associated with Morning and Evening respectively.<br /> <br /> So that leaves Neber-Het (Nephthys) as the most major deity not currently covered who will hopefully be one of the additional gods in the Companion.<br /> <br /> Other gods it would be cool to see who are lower priority: Bes, Renenutet, Satet, Anuket, Imsety, Hapi, Duamutef, Qebesenuef, Nekhbet, Wadjet, Wepwawet, Kebechet, Taweret, Seshat, Serqet, Imhotep, Neith<br /> <br /> And as I mentioned before, Khons makes a strong candidate for Titan, what with the Cannibal Hymn and all...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-11-2017, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T18:35:56-07:00","id":1128286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1127470#post1127470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Just went back to check - it's ambiguous. It says that Djehuty brokered enough extra moonlight for the extra days. It does make it sound on brief glance like he was being brokered with for the time, but actually then it would say &amp;quot;the Goddess (Nut) brokered enough extra moonlight&amp;quot; but it says &amp;quot;the God&amp;quot; (Djehuty). So he was brokering with someone on her behalf - which would presumably be Khonsu.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is ambiguous but I think you are right.<br /> <br /> As I was thinking about Djehuty and khonsu being the same god or not, i had a thought. Gods can have mantels but can Titans also have them? <br /> <br /> Could a god have a mantle that is a Titan or could a titan have a god mantle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3495-elroar","name":"Elroar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3495_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T09:42:22-07:00","id":1128492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1124364-kickstarter-update-chargen-and-revised-netjer?p=1127230#post1127230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit I snickered at the note saying that the biggest romantic difficulty that Scions of Het-Heru have comes from having too many loves at once, mostly since in the Exalted game I'm in that could apply to both my character and another PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like an amazingly wonderful situation looking for a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}